# hurl-workbench

> A Haskell-powered Hurl workbench for composing, exploring, executing, and testing reusable API workflows without duplicating request templates.

## Layout

This project is split into two cabal packages:

- **`hurl-workbench-core`** — the reusable library. The starter
  `HurlWorkbench.greet` function is called by the CLI, and the project-wide
  `HurlWorkbench.Prelude` re-exports
  [`lens`](https://hackage.haskell.org/package/lens) and
  [`generic-lens`](https://hackage.haskell.org/package/generic-lens).
- **`hurl-workbench-cli`** — the command-line interface. Exposes parser types,
  `parserInfo`, and `HurlWorkbench.Cli.runCli`, and ships an executable named
  **`hurl-workbench`**. Its Tasty suite checks the core behavior
  and parses the starter command without mutating process arguments.

Both packages use **GHC `ghc9124`** by default and expose **GHC 9.14.1** as a
secondary shell. They use `default-language: GHC2024` and the same warning set + default extensions
(`DeriveAnyClass`, `DuplicateRecordFields`, `OverloadedLabels`, `OverloadedStrings`).
Each package contains its own `LICENSE` and `CHANGELOG.md`, so `cabal check` and source
distributions do not depend on parent-directory paths.

## Develop

The project ships a Nix flake (`nix-haskell-flake`) that pins GHC and provides
the dev shell. Enter the shell with:

```bash
nix develop                # GHC ghc9124 with HLS
nix develop .#ghc9141      # current stable GHC compatibility shell
```

To add dev-shell tools or extra flake outputs, copy `flake.module.nix.example` to
`flake.module.nix` and edit it. It is imported automatically and is never overwritten
by template upgrades, so your customizations there survive `nix-haskell-flake` updates.

Then build and run:

```bash
cabal build all
cabal test all
cabal run hurl-workbench -- hello --name world
```

The flake exposes both packages and chooses the CLI executable as the default package.
It also runs the test suite as a flake check.

```bash
nix build                         # same as .#hurl-workbench-cli
nix build .#hurl-workbench-core
nix flake check
nix fmt -- --ci .
```

